# LIVE Python copy and runtime sequence review

Seven Python runtime modules were copied from the frozen v3 preparation directory. Only four literal gates changed from True to False. The other three modules remain byte-identical. All copied modules parsed successfully without importing or executing them. No device, ADB, USB, SSH or VM operation and no real write request was created. Python enablement is not a substitute for the separate native build and exact runtime request review.

The intended sequence is: construct the fixed adapter with an explicit unset cancellation event and a finite phase deadline; acquire the fixed remote lock once; upload and independently verify the three fixed helpers once; measure the native read-only occupancy gate; obtain full fresh evidence. B/misc original restoration must precede the cold NO_WRITE_NEEDED evidence required by directory fresh_gate and session. Stage and backup are separately bounded phases; activation uses fresh current-boot evidence, exact full inventories/Mac tar and its reviewed request. The final boot backend requires the exact real directory adapter and shares its cancellation object and a deadline within its boot budget.

Runtime conditions that must be handled explicitly:

- occupancy, inspect, fresh_gate and stage depend on the scanner already existing and passing its full SHA check. Calling them before helper provisioning fails closed.
- acquire and helper provisioning are exclusive creation operations, with no retry or automatic release. If a lock/helper already exists, do not call creation again. A separately reviewed continuation must verify the existing same-transaction owner and full helper hashes. A different owner is a stop condition.
- Any interrupted transport or unreadable acknowledgement persists UNKNOWN across new instances. A new folder or process does not clear it. The recovery-only grant permits original B/misc writes, not helper uploads or directory moves. If the pinned old native helper is missing after a reboot, that grant alone cannot bootstrap it; stop for separate review.
- Native occupancy may return UNKNOWN because a process naturally exits; this is not proof of a device hang. It is also not permission to retry automatically. Its actual latency/process churn acceptance remains a root-only read-only calibration gate.
- There are 512 raw-rootfs 4 MiB chunks plus other stage files; the per-phase budget must account for scan/readback overhead. No source change here claims the target can complete within its budget. Cold evidence must still be valid at actual rename and boot admission.
- Only gates changed. Some inherited __main__/exception strings still describe preparation or disabled operation. They are not execution-state evidence; the exact source manifest and actual gate values govern. There is no new command-line execution interface.

No source logic was changed in response to this sequence review. All unresolved conditions must be checked by the root operator and the independent reviewer before invoking the applicable API.
